{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Record Stage Positions}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Record_Stage_Positions}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Record Stage Positions
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Position List:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 A list of stage positions called \uldb \b Stage Points List\plain\b\fs24 {\v 139NVAW}\plain\fs24   may be maintained in memory.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 The data saved will be the position of each stage axis, the working distance, the magnification and the beam shift distance (i.e. beam offset distance).
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 Mark:
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \plain\fs24 This function causes the current stage position and associated data to be entered into the Stage Points List but without a label. 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 The label is \b M_\plain\fs24  is entered with an automatically incremented number.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\} Note that this function is also available as a special \ul Macro\plain\fs24 {\v 1815F7K@leom.hlp} function.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Label:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 This function brings up a Label Request Dialog box into which the user may type any string of text to identify the current stage position. 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \b OK\plain\fs24  will enter the position and label into the list. 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \b Cancel\plain\fs24  will remove the Label Request Dialog box without action.
\par \pard\tx355 \b 
\par \pard\tx355 Goto:
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \plain\fs24 The stage may be moved to positions in the list using the \b First, Next\plain\fs24  and \b Previous\plain\fs24  functions.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b On Goto:\plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 When moving to a stored position the \b working distance\plain\fs24  and \b magnification\plain\fs24  may be optionally set to the values stored at that point by marking these functions in the menu line \{bmc bm1.bmp\}.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \b Move XY Only. \plain\fs24 If this is selected \{bmc bm1.bmp\}. only the XY co-ordinates of a point are used for the move.  This does not apply to \ul Global Labels\plain\fs24 {\v Global_Labels}
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
