{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Calculate Scan}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Calculate_Scan}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Calculate Scan
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This function performs the following calculation.
\par 
\par The field of view is determined from the current magnification (i.e. the physical dimensions on the specimen of the image in normal mode)
\par 
\par The field of view is used with the \b Field Overlap\plain\fs24  to determine the \b Field Offset\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par Using the \b Stage Scan Start Position\plain\fs24 , the \b Stage Scan End position\plain\fs24  and the \b Field Offset\plain\fs24  the \b Number of Fields\plain\fs24  is determined.
\par 
\par See also \uldb \b Stage Scan Fields\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Scan_Fields}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
