\par 
\par \f6\fs24 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul \ul\fs20 Click\plain\f6\fs20 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP}\fs24  with the right mouse button to open the pop up menu \{bmc bm17.bmp\}.\f7\fs20 
\par 
\par \f6\fs24 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Select \b Quit Map\plain\f6\fs24   \b <Q>\plain\f6\fs24  to terminate the \b Stage Map\plain\f6\fs24  function.\f7\fs20 
\par 
\par \f6\fs24 \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab Note that any positions recorded are preserved and may be saved/used by the \uldb \b\fs20 Store / Recall\plain\f6\b\fs20 {\v 139NVAW}\plain\f6\fs24  functions.\f7\fs20 
\par 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Compucentric control}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Compucentric_control}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Compucentric Rotation}
\f2\b\fs36\cf1 Stage Compucentric control
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 The optional licenced Compucentric Control Software is designed to allow eucentric tilt and rotation stage movements by  computed corrections for the movements of the relevant axes.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Functions provided are:
\par \pard\tx355 \ul \ul Compucentric Rotation\plain\fs24 {\v Compucentric_Rotation}
\par \pard\tx355 \ul \ul Compucentric Tilt\plain\fs24 {\v Compucentric_Tilt}
\par \pard\tx355 \ul \ul Stage Horizontal alignment\plain\fs24 {\v Stage_Horizontal_alignment}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Compucentric movement is performed using the \uldb SEM Control Stage Tab\plain\fs24 {\v KH.ZCT@tabmgr.hlp}, selecting the Compucentric mode required.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Before compucentric functions can be used calibration is required.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Calibration is divided into two parts. First the rotation centre must be found which is sufficient for compucentric rotation and Stage Horizontal Alignment (stage tilt = 0). This will normally only need to be performed once each time the stage is serviced. However to achieve the ultimate accuracy it may be necessary to recalibrate the rotation centre each time the stage is initialised.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 To allow compucentric tilt (or compucentric rotate with a tilted stage) it is necessary to determine the specimen thickness, which is performed by the Compucentric Setup Wizard. Clearly this must be done each time the specimen is changed for one which has a different thickness.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 See Also 
\par \pard\tx355 \uldb Calibrate Stage centre of rotation\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_82@dlgmgr.hlp} 
\par \pard\tx355 \uldb Compucentric Setup\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_83@dlgmgr.hlp}.
\par \pard\tx355 \uldb Stage Horizontal Alignment dialog\plain\fs24 {\v 4YI0_84@dlgmgr.hlp}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Control Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Control_Overview}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Control Overview
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \f6 The stage is controlled either via the\uldb \b  joystick\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v QGFYFC@joystick.hlp}\plain\f6\fs24   or by \uldb \b ARROW Keys\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v 1ABTKON@Sem.HLP}.
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \f6 Initially the stage is in Joystick mode, Arrow Key Mode is only possible when the stage has been \uldb \b initialised\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Initialise}\plain\f6\fs24 .
\par \uldb \b Centre Point\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Centre_Point}\plain\f6\fs24   provides an alternative method of moving the stage to position a feature in the centre of the image.
\par 
\par \uldb \b Centre Feature\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Centre_Feature}\plain\f6\fs24  moves a selected area into the centre of the field of view and increases the magnification so that it fills the image area.
\par \pard 
\par \uldb \b Store / Recall\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v 139NVAW}\plain\f6\fs24  functions are provided which administer a memory list of stage positions which may also be saved to or loaded from file.
\par 
\par \uldb \b Stage Limits\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Limits}\plain\f6\fs24  may be set by the user.
\par 
\par \uldb \b Stage Registration\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Registration}\plain\f6\fs24  User defined co-ordinate systems
\par \uldb \b Stage Compucentric control\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Compucentric_control} 
\par \uldb Survey Mode\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v 4_DGYJ5@tabmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par \uldb \f6\b Stage Scan\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Scan} \plain\f6\fs24 moves the stage in a preselected raster.
\par \uldb \b Stage Map\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Map} \plain\f6\fs24 moves the stage to preselected positions.
\par \pard 
