{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Initialise}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Initialise}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Initialise
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par Stage initialisation is the process by which the stage control system identifies the current position of the stage relative to its limits. Therefore any function requiring absolute stage movement is disabled until the stage has been initialised. 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab From the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  call \b Stag\plain\b\fs24 e\plain\fs24  with \b <ALT + G>\plain\fs24  and then \b Stage I\plain\b\fs24 nitialise\plain\fs24  with \b <I>\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par The stage will then be driven until it reaches its limits which is at a known position. 
\par \pard\tx355 \ul \ul Detailed Sequence\plain\fs24 {\v _.YOE.@tabmgr.hlp}
\par \page
