{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Limits Overview}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Limits_Overview}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Limits Overview
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par Each axis (with the exception of the Rotate Axis) has the following limits.
\par 
\par \fs28 Physical limits:\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \b \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\tab Low Outer limit\plain\fs24  - a physical limit switch - hitting this loses stage position
\par 
\par \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\b \tab Low Inner limit\plain\fs24  - a physical limit switch - hitting this should not lose stage position (depends on speed of travel on impact)
\par 
\par \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\b \tab High Inner limit\plain\fs24  - a physical limit switch or soft limit defining extent of travel - no loss of stage position on impact
\par 
\par \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\b \tab High Outer limit\plain\fs24  - a physical limit switch - loses position on impact
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The Rotate axis optionally has a limit switch. This is only used during initialisation to register position. For all other purposes the limit is not used and the rotation is continuous.\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \fs28 User set limits:\b 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \b \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\tab Low User limit\plain\fs24   - a user defined limit to avoid specimen collisions- no loss of stage position on impact
\par 
\par \{bmc bm12.bmp\}\b \tab High User limit\plain\fs24  - a User defined limit to avoid specimen collisions - no loss of stage position on impact
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Map}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Map}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Map
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 The Stage Map function enables a frozen image in zone 0 to be used as a map for selecting stage positions.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab Call \b Stage\plain\fs24  from the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  with \b <ALT + G>\plain\fs24  and then call \b Stage Map\plain\fs24  with \b <A>\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par To use this function :
\par 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Select \b Scanning \plain\fs24 with \b <ALT + S>\plain\fs24  and then \uldb \b Split Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1QEXFRQ@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  with \b <P>\plain\fs24  form the Menu Bar.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Adjust the stage position and a low magnification such that the required area of the specimen is wholly displayed.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Freeze Zone 0.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Select \b Stage Map\plain\fs24  from the Menu Bar or \uldb \b Recall Dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Recall_Dialog}\plain\fs24  from the pop up menu when pressing the right mouse button in the image window when Stage Map is active..
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 This will cause the current stage position and magnification to be saved for the map.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The magnification may now be increased and the other live zone used to observe features of interest.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The mouse may be used to select a point on the 'map' and the stage (and hence live image) moved to the required position.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The \uldb \b Store / Recall\plain\b\fs24 {\v 139NVAW}\plain\fs24  functions may be used to save and recall positions.
\par \pard\li275\tx355 
\par \pard\li275\tx355 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The map is removed using \uldb \b Stage Close Map\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Close_Map}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
