{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Points List Box}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Points_List_Box}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Points List Box
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \f6 A list box displays (in alphanumeric order) the currently stored position labels.\f2 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \f6 To indicate if the stage is currently positioned at the highlighted entry the legend \b actioned!\plain\f6\fs24  will be displayed next to the text entry window when this is the case.\f2 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \f6\b Global Labels\plain\f6\fs24  may have been set which will list the stage position in all individual stage points lists. The label is starting with \b $\plain\f6\fs24 . \f2 
\par \pard\tx355 \f6 They may be used for such things as  the specimen exchange position. These Global Labels will therefore be listed in addition to the users specific stage points.\f2 
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The current points list in memory will be saved in the current \b User Directory\plain\fs24  on \b Log Off\plain\fs24  or if the user directory is changed. 
\par \pard\tx355 When a User Directory is selected the current points list file in that User Directory is loaded.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 There is a Global Points List maintained which is independent of the User Directory.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Global Labels ($...) may only be created/modified/deleted by users with \b Supervisor\plain\fs24  privilege.
\par \pard\tx355 \f6\b  \plain\fs24 
\par \page
