\b\fs36\cf1 Stage Points List File
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par The list may be saved to file or the contents of the list replaced from a file using the load function.
\par    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-6 \cellx7015\cellx7795\cellx9995\pard\intbl\tx355 \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b File\plain\fs24  to open the menu.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Select \b Load \plain\fs24 to enter the standard loading dialog to load a list from the User Directory. \f6 This function loads the Coordinate List from a previously saved file. The current list of position data is deleted.\f2 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \f7\fs20 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \f6\fs24 From the \b Select Coordinate File\plain\f6\fs24  dialog select the file name from the User Directory. The extension is \b *.XYZ\plain\f6\fs24 .\f7\fs20 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \f6\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl \f2 \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Select \uldb \b Save As\plain\b\fs24 {\v Save_Coordinate_File}\plain\fs24  to save the active list to the User Directory.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \f6 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \f2 \{bmc bm21.bmp\}\f6 \cell\intbl\row
\pard \f2 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Click on \b Clear List\plain\fs24  to empty the actual Stage Points List.
\par 
\par \f6 The current base \b magnification\plain\f6\fs24  is saved whenever an entry is made into the position list.\f2 
\par 
\par \f6 The current \b working distance\plain\f6\fs24  is saved whenever an entry is made into the position list. \f2 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Points List Goto}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Points_List_Goto}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Points List Goto
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par In the \b Goto\plain\fs24  frame 4 different buttons to move the stage are shown:
\par 
\par \b First: \plain\f6\fs24 This function causes the stage to move to the position defined by the first entry in the Stage Points List.\f2 
\par 
\par \b Next:\plain\fs24  This function causes the stage to move to the position defined by the next entry in the \f6 Stage Points List\f2 .
\par 
\par \b Previous:\plain\fs24  This function causes the stage to move to the position defined by the previous entry in the \f6 Stage Points List\f2 .
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \b Selected:\plain\fs24  This function causes the stage to move to the position defined by the highlighted entry in the \f6 Stage Points List\f2 .
\par 
\par \ul \b\ul Undo Stage Goto\plain\b\fs24 {\v IDQXIJ@tabmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm7.bmp\}\tab Since Global Labels are not part of the user's list they are ignored in  \b Goto First\plain\fs24 , \b Next\plain\fs24  and \b Previous\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm8.bmp\} First, Next and Previous: These apply to the chronological order in which they were generated, not to the alphabetical order in which the points are listed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Points List On Goto}
