\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Recall Dialog
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par This function causes the current stage position and magnification to be saved for the map.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\}\tab The \uldb \b Stage Map Conditions\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Map}\plain\fs24  should have previously been setup
\par 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The magnification may now be increased and the other live zone used to observe features of interest.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The mouse may be used to select a point on the 'map' and the stage (and hence live image) moved to the required position.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\} \b Plot Positions\plain\fs24  displays a black dot on the stage window for each position stored in the list.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\}\b  Hide Positions\plain\fs24  hides the dots marked by Plot Positions.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm14.bmp\} The \uldb \b Store / Recall\plain\b\fs24 {\v 139NVAW}\plain\fs24  functions may be used to save and recall positions.
