{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Scan Commands}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Scan_Commands}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Scan Commands
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par There are three commands provided:
\par 
\par \b Start Stage Scan\plain\fs24  
\par This moves the stage to the start position and sets the scan status to \b at field\plain\fs24 .
\par You can also use the cursor key labelled \{bmc bm23.bmp\} together with the Shift key \{bmc bm9.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \b Stage Next Field\plain\fs24  
\par This moves to the next field in the scan pattern. If the current field is the last field in the pattern the stage is not moved but the scan status is set to \b end scan\plain\fs24 .
\par You can also use the cursor key labelled \{bmc bm24.bmp\} together with the Shift key \{bmc bm9.bmp\}.
\par \pard 
\par \b Stage Previous Field\plain\fs24  
\par This moves to the previous field in the scan pattern. If the current field is the first field in the pattern the stage is not moved but the scan status is set to \b end scan\plain\fs24 .
\par You can also use the cursor key labelled \{bmc bm25.bmp\} together with the Shift key \{bmc bm9.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.bmp\} Note that commands may be included in \uldb \b macros\plain\b\fs24 {\v 2D05Z_N@LeoM.HLP}\plain\fs24 .
\par \page
