{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Scan Fields}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Scan_Fields}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Stage Initialize}
\b\fs36\cf1 Stage Scan Fields
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \b Stage Scan Start Position
\par \plain\fs24 These are the X, Y and Z positions at which the stage scan will start.
\par The stage will move to this position on execution of the \b Stage\plain\fs24  \b Start scan\plain\fs24  command.
\par The values may be defined manually (\ul click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on the parameter field), by the \uldb \b Select Area\plain\b\fs24 {\v Select_Scan_Area}\plain\fs24  button or by the \uldb \b Stage Scan Start here\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Scan_Start_here}\plain\fs24  button,
\par 
\par \b Field Offset (Field Size)
\par \plain\fs24 The X and Y field Offset parameters define the distance the stage will step between fields.
\par \pard The values may be defined manually, or will be entered by the \uldb \b Stage Calculate Scan\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Calculate_Scan}\plain\fs24  function.
\par 
\par \b Fields
\par \plain\fs24 The X and Y fields parameters define the number of fields the stage will step in the appropriate direction for the scan pattern
\par The values may be defined manually, or will be entered by the \b Stage\plain\fs24  \b Calculate Scan\plain\fs24  function.
\par \b    \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-6 \cellx7585\cellx8085\cellx12265\pard\intbl \b Stage Scan End coordinates
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 This is the X Y position which will be used in the \b Stage\plain\fs24  \b Calculate Scan\plain\fs24  function and defines the position at which the stage scan will end.
\par\intbl The values may be defined manually, by the \b Select area\plain\fs24  button or by the \uldb \b Stage Scan End here\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Scan_End_here}\plain\fs24  button,
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b Field Overlap
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 
\par\intbl This parameter may be set  manually and is used in the \b Stage\plain\fs24  \b Calculate Scan\plain\fs24  function to determine the amount of overlap between fields. A field overlap of 0% will result in a set of fields which butt together.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \b \{bmc bm26.wmf\}\plain\fs24 \cell\intbl\row
\pard \b 
\par \page
