{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Scan Status Information}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Stage_Scan_Status_Information}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Stage Scan Status Information
\par \pard \plain\fs24    
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-6 \cellx7015\cellx14035\pard\intbl \b At Field\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl The X and Y \b At Field\plain\fs24  parameters define at which field the stage is currently positioned. These parameters may be used as annotation so that the correct field identity may be identified in saved images.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b Stage Scan Invalid\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl This indicates if the current stage scan pattern is invalid or not.
\par\intbl The scan will be invalid if the combination of scan parameters would take the stage beyond the \uldb \b user defined stage limits\plain\b\fs24 {\v Stage_Limits}\plain\fs24  (in X, Y or Z)
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b Stage scanning\plain\fs24 
\par\intbl This parameter indicates the current state of stage scanning.\par\pard \pard\intbl\li275\tx355 \b Idle\plain\fs24  \tab Stage scan has not been started
\par\intbl \b At Field\plain\fs24  \tab Stage is positioned at a field in the scan pattern
\par\intbl \b Moving\plain\fs24  \tab The stage is in motion as a result of a Next Field or Previous Field command.
\par\intbl \b At End\plain\fs24  \tab The scan pattern has been completed.\cell\pard \pard\intbl\li275\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm13.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \pard\tx355 \tab 
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Store / Recall}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 139NVAW}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Stage Limits;Stage Points List ADD}
\b\fs36\cf1 Store / Recall
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\f7\fs20 
\par \pard\tx355 \f6\fs24 A list of stage positions may be maintained in memory. The entries are shown in the \b Stage Points List\plain\f6\fs24 . Initially this list is empty. \f2 The data saved is the current position of the stage. If beam shift is being applied the XY stage position is modified by the Beam Offset distance to give a stage XY position with zero beam shift. Also saved are the current working distance and magnification. When moving to a stored position the beam shift is set to zero and optionally either or both of the magnification/working distance are set to the saved values\f6 .\f2 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-6 \cellx7015\cellx7795\cellx13235\pard\intbl\tx355 \f6\fs20 
\par\intbl \fs24 The list can be called by:
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab From the \uldb \b Menu Bar\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v 8ZP0K4@Sem.HLP}\plain\f6\fs24  call \b Stage\plain\f6\fs24  with \b <ALT + G>\plain\f6\fs24  and then \b Store / Recall\plain\f6\fs24  with \b <R>\plain\f6\fs20 
\par\intbl \fs24 
\par\intbl or
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm2.bmp\}\tab From the Menu Bar call \b Tools\plain\f6\fs24  with \b <ALT + T>\plain\f6\fs24  and then \ul click\plain\f6\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b Goto Panel\plain\f6\fs24 . From the \ul Drop-down List\plain\f6\fs24 {\v XYVXW3@Sem.HLP} select \b Stage Points List\plain\f6\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Stage positions may be used in \uldb \b macros\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v 5XK5S7@LeoM.HLP}\plain\f6\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm14.bmp\} Close the panel with \{bmc bm15.bmp\}.
\par\intbl \fs20 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 \fs24 Positions with the prefix $ are Global Positions and are common for all users (example\b  $Exchange\plain\f6\b\fs24 {\v _Exchange})\plain\f6\fs24 .\par\pard \pard\intbl For additional information point to the item of interest on the picture to the right. \cell\pard \pard\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm28.shg\}\fs20 
\par\intbl \fs24 When the cursor changes from \{bmc bm29.bmp\}to \{bmc bm30.bmp\}help is available. Click to present the information.\cell\intbl\row
\pard \fs20 
\par \page
